      "created_at": "2013-04-17T20:48:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>We know what card is next in the deck. :) Since it is a co-op game it isn't much of an issue. Also kepe in mind, your starting 8 cards have a back, only the Station cards don't.</p><p>EDIT: When I shuffle, I don't look at the cards, so that they would be shuffled. You would still know what card is on top of your deck though.</p><p>EDIT2: Well I guess I was wrong this whole time:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Quoting Megatone from this link:</p><p><a href=\"http://boardgamegeek.com/thread/963503/my-experience-playing-an-early-prototype\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://boardgamegeek.com/thread/963503/my-experience-playing-an-early-prototype</a></p><p>\"At the stage the game was at when I played it, yes. I asked Christopher about that specifically because I felt like I was cheating at first and was trying to shuffle under the table. He confirmed that it was by design.\"</p>",
