    {
      "id": 60286,
      "name": "Pydro",
      "username": "Pydro",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/{size}/1844_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-04-17T20:56:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Spiff\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/48/1865_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Spiff:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So, at all times you know which three station cards are in play and which will be in play next once a spot opens up, yes?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yes. you know the top card of the Station deck at all times.</p>\n<p>EDIT: This is an important part of the strategy. There are only ever 3 cards availabe to purchase from each Sector. However, once you purchase a card another card moves into the Sector (so you always have 3). Knowing what card comes next is very important, because once it is inplay it is inplay.</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:36:17.802Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
