      "id": 60287,
      "name": "Cosmonaut Zero",
      "username": "Cosmonaut_Zero",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/cosmonaut_zero/{size}/2520_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-04-17T23:08:38.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Shuffling the station deck seems fine to me. I've played other games where you can see the top card of a deck. In Eminent Domain, for example, you can know what type of planet is on top of the planet deck, and how much it takes to settle or attack. And that doesn't feel that strange.</p><p>If station cards get shuffled into your own deck, that seems like it would feel really weird. You can know where cards are in your deck, and the temptation to shuffle until the order looks good to you (or at least you have what you need in your next hand) would be immense.</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:36:17.878Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
