      "raw": "I've pitched in the pt forums that instead of Shuffling you construct and stack your deck each time it needs to be reset.  This allows you to plan how things are going to turn out,  which when you get into the guts of the game is what it's all about - planning for the optimal play. \r\n\r\nthat said the way it is now let's you do so on a limited scale.  I think it's just part of the game because of the two sided card design choice.  There is no way to really prevent it,  other than asking your buddy for a random cut,  and it is somewhat emphasized by the aspect of turn planning that's involved.",
